index 0000000..812553f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-review.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# Privacy and integration review
+
+Review date: 2026-10-19. This is a code and automated HTTP review, not an independent security certification. No manual browser verification was performed.
+
+## Data inventory
+
+| Data | Purpose | Storage and retention | User control |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Random session identifier | Associate explicitly saved articles with this browser | First-party HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax cookie; Secure and __Host prefix in production; 24-hour maximum age | Delete reading list or remove last item |
+| Up to 100 saved article IDs | Reading list only | Bounded process memory; expiry within 24 hours of the last mutation; cleared on restart; no disk persistence | Export JSON, remove individual entries, delete entire list |
+| Connection metadata | Deliver the requested page/resource | Host/proxy controlled; application adds no request, credential, or reading-list logging | Operator must publish actual hosting log retention |
+
+Anonymous reads do not initialize sessions. Article IDs are validated against published content; input size is bounded at 1 KiB and personal responses cannot be cached publicly. No user accounts, credentials, browsing history, analytics, fingerprint, or device permissions are collected by application code. This does not eliminate hosting access logs.
+
+## Third-party integration inventory
+
+| Integration found | Exposure before review | Disposition |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Cloud Functions analytics client | Runs on every page, including credential forms; can access page content | Removed; no replacement tracker |
+| Cloud Functions account APIs | Username and password sent directly to an external demo service | Disabled; forms replaced with an honest availability notice; requires a reviewed backend before restoration |
+| Google Fonts | Visitor IP and request metadata exposed via preconnect/styles/font requests | Removed; local serif fallback |
+| Imgur editorial images | Visitor IP and metadata; article page used credentialed image requests | Replaced with existing bundled editorial photos; credentialed image behavior removed |
+| Cinemai thumbnail | Cross-origin image request | Replaced with existing local photo |
+| Advertising queue | DOM references exposed to a global third-party queue | Removed; static spacing retained |
+| External editorial link | Connects only after user navigation | Kept as an ordinary hyperlink; no-referrer policy |
+| Hosting platform | Connection metadata and any operator access logs | Required; operator must review log access, redaction, retention, backups, and TLS |
+
+Content schema and image utilities reject remote editorial images. CSP restricts resource loading to this origin and blocks frames, objects, cross-origin connections and framing. Astro supplies hashes for framework inline scripts/styles. Ordinary page navigation replaces ClientRouter because Astro's hash-based CSP does not support it. No reporting collector is introduced: raw CSP reports may include private page URLs; add one only with redaction, access controls, and explicit short retention. Trusted Types enforcement is deferred until framework hydration sinks are assessed; no permissive default policy is installed.
+
+## Repeatable checks
+
+Run before each release and whenever a dependency or integration changes:
+
+```sh
+pnpm audit:privacy
+pnpm build
+pnpm test:privacy
+pnpm audit --prod
+```
+
+`audit:privacy` flags external URLs in runtime source, browser storage access, fingerprinting patterns, analytics beacons, and scripts in editorial content. It is a conservative review guard, not a general JavaScript security analyzer. HTTP tests check all article pages for direct external image/script requests and valid CSP script hashes, private headers, no cookies during anonymous reading, input rejection, cross-site access denial, cookie flags, isolation between clients, export, removal, and deletion with old-cookie replay. HTTP checks do not execute JavaScript or observe runtime network behavior.
+
+The production dependency audit on the review date reported zero known vulnerabilities. Audit results change as new advisories are published; re-run rather than relying on this record.
+
+## Adding a service
+
+The maintainer must record its owner, purpose, exact endpoints, fields transmitted (including IP/referrer/cookies), consent model, retention, deletion support, subprocessors, contract/security evidence, and next review date in this inventory. Review at least quarterly and on every service change. Obtain independent security/privacy review before restoring credential collection or introducing sensitive-data processing; retain the report and track findings to closure. This repository does not claim such a review has occurred.
+
+Keep optional services unloaded by default. If an optional embed is approved, use a locally hosted preview and an explicit user action before contacting its provider, with an equally usable decline path. Do not send reading lists or credentials to analytics. Version and integrity-pin necessary immutable external scripts, keep them off sensitive pages, and deliberately amend the resource policy and regression checks after review.
+
+## Deployment requirements
+
+- Set `APP_ORIGIN` to the deployed public origin before building when using a new hostname; only explicitly configured hosts are trusted for origin checks.
+- Serve production through HTTPS. Production session cookies will not work over plain HTTP (local `pnpm dev` uses a development cookie).
+- Start HSTS at 300 seconds for this host. Increase only after verifying HTTPS routing; do not add subdomain or preload commitments without reviewing those hosts.
+- Preserve application security headers at the proxy; apply equivalent resource/permissions/referrer policy to static assets served directly by the CDN. Personalized responses must never enter shared caches.
+- The ephemeral session driver supports one process. For multiple replicas, use a reviewed shared store with real automatic deletion, authenticated TLS, encryption at rest, and access controls; preserve the 24-hour limit. Existing filesystem sessions from a previous deployment are not migrated: purge the old `.astro/sessions` store and any copies/backups under the operator's retention process.
+- Restrict and redact hosting/proxy logs. Do not log bodies, cookies, credentials, full private URLs, or reading lists. Record and publish the host's actual metadata retention before handling production traffic.
+- Recheck actual deployed headers, TLS, storage expiry and access controls after deployment. Automated source/HTTP tests cannot certify the hosting environment or replace independent audits.
